1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Hello everyone, the CLOSE 2024.1 version is about to meet you.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The new features are fully upgraded to make your experience more convenient.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
This video will take you through a new version of the update from the point of view of clothing development.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Including UI updates, file preparation, file editing, design, production, display, and the final one-stop cooperation in the Closet.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Without further ado, let's take a look.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
First of all, we have optimized the UI.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,000
One of the biggest changes is that in the main menu at the top, you will now see the option to produce, connect, and Closet.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Therefore, you can directly visit here or upload files to Closet.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
You can upload project files, clothing, or virtual models.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
After the file has been modified, you can also upload the updated version.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
If you need to use the Everywhere function and upload files,

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
you can find it in the Connect option.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You can also see that the Everywhere UI has been updated.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
In the production option, you can find the function of coloring, material list, and checking the code.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
In the material, you can find the material generator.

16
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
In the virtual model, you can find the virtual model editor and other related functions.

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
In addition, in the library window, we have added a new virtual model file folder, Mantel Human.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
You can directly double-click to import and use Closet.

19
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
At the moment, we do not support directly editing the size in Closet.

20
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:37,000
You can choose to change the size and gender of the Mantel Human virtual model in the map window on the left.

21
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Regarding virtual models,

22
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Connect has also updated some faceless children virtual models.

23
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
You can edit the size of them in the virtual model editor.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
In the new version, the UI of the virtual model editor has also been updated.

25
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
First of all, you can use the single click to drag the virtual model to the actual line.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
To change the measurement position and the measurement value.

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
After the adjustment, you can also right-click to reset the position or reset all positions.

28
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
In this way, we can adjust the size according to the need to edit these measurement values.

29
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,000
In the right editor, you can set different types of measurement values that you want to check or hide.

30
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
In the width size, you can set a total width first.

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
For example, set a lower-body size.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
You can also choose whether to set the width value.

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
You can set the width value and the measurement value of the width below to be linked.

34
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Linking means that when adjusting the total width value,

35
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
the measurement value below will be adjusted to a certain extent to adapt to the total width.

36
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Then you can adjust the size of the chest again,

37
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
so that the outline of the chest is more natural and real.

38
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
In addition, you can now control the width of the female and male models,

39
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
which is to adjust the width between the thighs of the legs,

40
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
to make them bigger or smaller.

41
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
In the male model bucket, you can change the width of the thighs,

42
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
and you can also change the size of the thighs.

43
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,000
In the same way, the male model can also drag the measurement line on the body to modify the size.

44
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Set up the virtual model.

45
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Next, we can import the costume for editing.

46
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Select a file in the close-up resource library.

47
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Right-click to open the previous version of this style,

48
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
and load it into the work area.

49
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Come to the 2D window, you can edit the version below.

50
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
First, switch to the black and white surface view,

51
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
find the sewing tool in the 2D tool bar,

52
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
then add a seam allowance to the seam allowance.

53
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
You can see that one of the updates is that the seam allowance will automatically be cut into the seam allowance.

54
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
This can be applied to larger seam allowance types.

55
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
If you want the seam allowance to display different types of seam allowance,

56
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
you just need to click on the seam allowance shortcut.

57
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
You can see that there are different folding types in the attribute editor download menu.

58
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
You can choose.

59
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Next, look at the back.

60
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
You can see that there is a basic line in the middle of the seam allowance at the bottom of the back piece.

61
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Therefore, now, even if you use the seam allowance transfer tool to turn the seam,

62
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
the new seam allowance in the middle will also retain the basic line.

63
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Continue to use the production source order line tool to adjust the bottom.

64
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Divide the panels,

65
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
then use the extension panel tool to extend the back piece.

66
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:17,000
The extension panel tool after the update can also be extended to the symmetrical panel,

67
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
