111
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
When you open it,

112
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:14,000
you will see that the color in the fabric will be more random.

113
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
You can also control the randomness

114
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
by sliding, sliding, or entering numbers.

115
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:23,000
You can also use random variables to get different results.

116
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
In addition,

117
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
the function of adjusting the direction of the wool is also added.

118
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
You can adjust the direction of the wool

119
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,000
by sliding, sliding, or entering numbers.

120
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
CLO supports sRGB format now.

121
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Open the sRGB sticker created by PS in CLO.

122
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
The color will be more consistent.

123
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Here, insert an inner top shirt,

124
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
and add sRGB stickers on it.

125
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
This sticker was created in PS.

126
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
At this time,

127
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
