128
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
and the color in PS remain the same height.

129
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
On the contrary,

130
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:00,000
the sRGB sticker from CLO is also the same color.

131
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Next, let's make a jeans.

132
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
A sticker is added to the jeans.

133
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Select the sticker,

134
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
you can see that the property editor

135
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
added a new option below the line chart.

136
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Use the same as the plant.

137
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Click on the button,

138
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
you can apply the hair line picture of the jeans fabric to the sticker.

139
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
After opening,

140
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
you can see that the sticker also applies the hair line effect of the jeans.

141
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
And if you select the jeans fabric,

142
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
adjust the hair line intensity,

143
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
the hair line effect of the sticker will also change.

144
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Below this picture,

145
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
transparent picture,

146
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
and other 3D stickers,

147
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:35,000
there is also an option to use the same as the plant.

148
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
In addition,

149
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
the sticker also adds a preset type.

150
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Click on the download menu,

151
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,000
you can see that the default is digital print.

152
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Then it is the uniform,

153
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
retrofitting,

154
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
and the gold.

155
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
The gold color can be modified.

156
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Choose to mix with the plant,

157
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,000
the sticker will apply all 3D stickers of the plant.

158
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
You can see that at this time,

159
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
the same options for using and planting

160
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
are in the open state below the 3D sticker.

161
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Another update about the sticker is

162
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
to click on the sticker in the object window,

163
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
the property editor can see that

164
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
there is no other 3D sticker,

165
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
there is only a texture picture at the moment.

166
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Click on the automatically generate button,

167
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,000
you can easily and quickly generate other 3D stickers,

168
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:24,000
and the generated stickers can be stored separately.

169
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:29,000
The plant can also use the option of automatically generating 3D stickers.

170
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Next,

171
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
let's take a look at the update about the color of the flag.

172
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
We have created a more diverse system,

173
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
so that you can set more color options flexibly.

174
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Now, when you add a flag color,

175
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
you can add a flag color that only adjusts to the material,

176
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
a flag color that only adjusts to all properties,

177
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,000
or you can set the information of the flag color of the related materials.

178
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
For example, you can create a flag color that only adjusts to the material,

179
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:00,000
you can modify the color, texture, and size.

180
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
You can also add ink,

181
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
and set the display of the sticker, etc.

182
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Or you can also choose

183
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
to set all the material properties of a flag color separately,

184
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,000
so that you can modify its texture information and physical properties separately.

185
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
By using the new flag color function,

186
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
you can use the above settings

187
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:28,000
to view and edit clothes more freely during the work process.

188
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
The measurement tool in the new version has also been optimized.

189
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:38,000
You can now switch between different modes by clicking the shortcut key P.

190
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
A mode is the one that allows you to change the color,

191
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
and a mode is the one that allows you to measure the length of the outside of the panel.

192
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
You can operate it along the outer outline of the panel,

193
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
just like the operation of the free sewing tool.

194
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Another mode is the straight line length measurement,

195
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
which is measured inside the panel.

196
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,000
You can also create a free straight line inside and outside the panel.

197
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
All measurement values will be displayed in the object window.

198
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Now you can also more conveniently edit the code of the sticker.

199
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
When you enter the code for the sticker,

200
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
use the edit code tool to select the sticker,

201
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
and in the attribute editor,

202
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
you can choose the number of percent or unit

203
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
to decide how to change the size of the code.

204
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
When using the number of percent,

205
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
you don't have to know exactly the size of each size of the sticker,

206
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
which is more convenient.

207
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Or use the edit code tool.

208
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Now you can do the inner line refitting on the panel

209
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
to achieve different ways of matching the code.

210
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
When looking at the code,

211
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
we added a full mirror mode,

212
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:42,000
which allows you to see all the sizes in one picture.

213
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:46,000
It is more convenient to observe the difference between the sizes.

214
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,000
You can adjust the rotation of the X-axis to see the angles of the clothes,

215
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
and you can also adjust the distance between each size.

216
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
And we can also use this mode

217
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:59,000
to see the pressure and force of the clothes.

218
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Finally, you can output the clothes rendering image.

219
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
